  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute To The Economic Recovery Of Iraq Through Employment Creation And Revitalisation Of Local Economies &#x2013; Phase VI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase VI, a 48-month programme, will channel its scope around multi-faceted interventions across communities in nine governorates of Iraq (Anbar, Baghdad, Diyala, Dohuk, Erbil, Kirkuk, Ninewa, Salah Al-Din, Sulaymaniyah) focusing on (1) improving community and stakeholder engagement through strengthened partnerships and capacity-building initiatives, (2) enhancing individual employability and micro-, small-, and medium-enterprise (MSME) sustainability through a) revitalized local economies, b) strengthened value chains, c) enhanced MSME business capabilities, d) improved job referral linkages between job seekers and employers, and e) increased access to finance among EDF businesses and similar enterprises across Iraq and (3) strengthening resilience and self-reliance of local producers to climate change and environmental degradation. The main objective of this project will be to contribute to the economic recovery and stabilization of Iraq through employment creation and revitalization of local economies which IOM plans to achieve through the application of an integral approach seeking to address key needs related to employment and income generation for IDPs, climate induced IDPs, returnees host communities, and other target groups in creating sustainable solutions for economic conditions in vulnerable communities.</narrative>
  </description>
